#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:96
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of acpid"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:99
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>acpid</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:103
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>./configure --prefix=/usr \\\n"
"            --docdir=/usr/share/doc/acpid-&acpid-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:108
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a test suite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:112
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:115
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>make install                         &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -m755 -d /etc/acpi/events &amp;&amp;\n"
"cp -r samples /usr/share/doc/acpid-&acpid-version;</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:122
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring acpid"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:125
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>acpid</application> is configured by user defined events.  "
"Place event files under <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/acpi/events</filename> directory. If an event "
"occurs, <command>acpid</command> recurses through the event files in order "
"to see if the regex defined after \"event\" matches. If they do, action is "
"executed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:134
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The following brief example will suspend the system when the laptop lid is "
"closed<phrase revision='sysv'> (it requires <xref linkend=\"pm-"
"utils\"/>)</phrase>.  The example also disables the default handling of the "
"lid close event by &logind; when the system is on battery and not connected "
"to any external monitor, in order to avoid a conflict:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:142
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/acpi/events/lid &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>event=button/lid\n"
"action=/etc/acpi/lid.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/acpi/lid.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>#!/bin/sh\n"
"/bin/grep -q open /proc/acpi/button/lid/LID/state &amp;&amp; exit 0\n"
"/usr/sbin/pm-suspend</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"chmod +x /etc/acpi/lid.sh\n"
"\n"
"mkdir -pv /etc/elogind/logind.conf.d\n"
"echo <literal>HandleLidSwitch=ignore</literal> &gt; /etc/elogind/logind.conf.d/acpi.conf</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:157
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/acpi/events/lid &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>event=button/lid\n"
"action=/etc/acpi/lid.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/acpi/lid.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>#!/bin/sh\n"
"/bin/grep -q open /proc/acpi/button/lid/LID/state &amp;&amp; exit 0\n"
"/usr/bin/systemctl suspend</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"chmod +x /etc/acpi/lid.sh\n"
"\n"
"mkdir -pv /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d\n"
"echo <literal>HandleLidSwitch=ignore</literal> &gt; /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/acpi.conf</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:173
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, not every computer labels ACPI events in the same way (for "
"example, the lid may be recognized as <filename>LID0</filename> instead of "
"<filename>LID</filename>).  To determine how your buttons are recognized, "
"use the <command>acpi_listen</command> tool. Also, look in the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">samples</filename> directory under <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/doc/acpid-&acpid-version;</filename> for more"
" examples."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:184
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<phrase revision=\"sysv\">Boot Script</phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\">Systemd Socket</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:188
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To automatically start <command>acpid</command> when the system is rebooted,"
" install the <filename>/etc/rc.d/init.d/acpid</filename> boot script from "
"the <xref linkend=\"bootscripts\"/> package."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:194
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To start the <command>acpid</command> daemon at boot, install the systemd "
"unit from the <xref linkend=\"systemd-units\"/> package by running the "
"following command as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:204
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install-acpid</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/acpid.xml:208
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This package uses socket based activation and will be started when something"
" needs it. No standalone unit file is provided for this package."
msgstr ""

